{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1475042-from-the-supernal","id":1475042,"title":"From the Supernal...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-20T09:05:00-08:00","id":1475042,"title":"From the Supernal...","content":"There was a discussion (again avoiding nercothreading) of a familiar/Artifact/retainer Merit mixture or 'living Artifact'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1456352-retainer-option-for-a-mage?p=1456483#post1456483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A living Artifact? But that doesn\u2019t <i>need</i> to be represented by the Artifact rules, right?<br /> <br /> I\u2019d have the retainer be a polymorphed Sleepwalker acolyte trying to get back to human form, using the Retainer rules with their field being \u201cbe an acolyte to mages.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div> (quoting partly to link back to that discussion).<br /> <br /> And someone definitely mentioned invisible entities.<br /> <br /> So. My question, how are &quot;living Artifact&quot;s and supernal beings distinguished?<br /> <br /> I mean, both are inherently supernal, both have Gnosis and Arcanum. One is normally very temporary, while the other seems to be inherently permanent.<br /> <br /> Could you weave an Artifact (below Archmastery) to make it living? Or cause it to become sentient? Not like fettering a ghost/spirit to it. But actually making an Artifact alive... <br /> <br /> What room is there in this space for interesting entities, whether as allies, antagonist, or pawns of Archmasters? <br /> <br /> Feels like you could have a lasting version of an Eidolon (and use it as a retainer?) Or a Golem-Artifact...<br /> <br /> EDIT:. this smells a bit like Alchemical Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-20-2022, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T09:32:34-08:00","id":1475046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1475042-from-the-supernal#post1475042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, both are inherently supernal, both have Gnosis and Arcanum. One is normally very temporary, while the other seems to be inherently permanent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernal beings have Rank instead of Gnosis. You're thinking of subsouls like Ochemata and Talismans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T11:41:21-08:00","id":1475052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1475042-from-the-supernal?p=1475046#post1475046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernal beings have Rank instead of Gnosis. You're thinking of subsouls like Ochemata and Talismans.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) what is a talisman? (All i can find is this: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Talisman\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Talisman</a> )<br /> <br /> And 2) Gnosis vs rank, seems like a difference without a distinction. What would the distinction be? <br /> <br /> Eg: Supernal beings can't create soul stones because they don't have Gnosis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T12:11:25-08:00","id":1475055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1475042-from-the-supernal?p=1475052#post1475052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) what is a talisman? (All i can find is this: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Talisman\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Talisman</a> )<br /> <br /> And 2) Gnosis vs rank, seems like a difference without a distinction. What would the distinction be?<br /> <br /> Eg: Supernal beings can't create soul stones because they don't have Gnosis?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) Its covered in the Imperial Mysteries book. A Talisman is like an Ochemata, a sub soul of its creator, but in the form of an Artifact. It has a mind of its own, Gnosis, objectives and the ability to use the Arcana. Normally you require an archmage with 8 dots in an Arcana or a Rank 8 Supernal Entity to cast, which normally translates to some of the most powerful beings in the Supernal or the mightiest Bound in the entire Tapestry.<br /> <br /> 2) There is a huge distinction. Gnosis is the intuitive connection the mage has to the Supernal Realms, which informs his views on reality and allows them to seek out and draw forth the correct symbols, superimposing them unto a target to overwrite reality. Rank is the property of a emphemeral entity, representing how well they embody whatever phenomenon they represent. Because they are not human, they do not have such a connection and therefore cannot create a soul stone. Gnosis is the command console for the universe's CPU that you need to somehow grok how to use, Rank represents how powerful the AI that oversees that part of the system is.<br /> <br /> However, should you wish for an alternative, albeit very hubristic alternative to making a soul stone, then I recommend taking a look at the <i>Summoners book</i>. I seem to remember a ritual to create one by binding an entity wholesale into a suitable vessel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T13:20:55-08:00","id":1475057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1475042-from-the-supernal?p=1475052#post1475052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) what is a talisman? (All i can find is this: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Talisman\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Talisman</a> )</div> </div> </div> </div>An Artifact that is also an archmage's subsoul, able to cast spells on its own; when Signs of Sorcery refers to the Watchtowers as &quot;symbol-realm-talismans,&quot; it's because of this bit from Imperial Mysteries' discussion of the Oracles:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Watchtowers have been examined by hundreds of archmages throughout history making pilgrimages to revisit their Awakening. <b>Each appears to be a Talisman of unknown owner, merged with and generating the Lustrum in which it sits, so that it serves as a refuge from being absorbed by the Supernal Realm.</b> The process by which they Awaken new mages from across the Abyss is unknown, but is taken by Siddha as evidence for the existence of the Practice of Assumption. Curiously, the Watchtowers <u>move</u>; they are never found in the same Lustrum twice, but have also never been seen mid-translocation. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And 2) Gnosis vs rank, seems like a difference without a distinction. What would the distinction be?<br /> <br /> Eg: Supernal beings can't create soul stones because they don't have Gnosis? </div> </div> </div>Reaching Gnosis 6 doesn't propel you to the level of power where your abilities and vulnerabilities exist at the level of plot-device for anyone who isn't also functionally a god; Supernal beings that aren't ochemata interact with spellcasting and the world in a very different way from, say, an ochema.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T18:44:43-08:00","id":1475072,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the replies, very informative. <br /> <br /> I think it i had a simple misunderstanding about Gnosis vs rank for supernal beings (i was also assuming they roll rank+ arcanum rather than power + finesse - my bad).<br /> <br /> And it kind makes sense for them not to have a connection to the supernal, if indeed they are manifestations of the supernal. <br /> <br /> As opposed to an Artifact which is also from the Supernal, but somehow meant to be here and connected via Gnosis (i wonder how this would affect the likelyhood that a supernal being would allow you to give them an Artifact to take back to the Supernal...)<br /> <br /> Still curious about ideas for Artifact creatures, Artifact-Golem seems cool (taking an Artifact and turning it into a Golem), also Artifact Guardian Keeper - working to keep one of the Bound in check. Other ideas would be a using some kind of 'living' Death Artifact to act as an artificial Kerboros in an artificial underworld.... Something something Hedge, Astral, awakened Cat Artifact...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T09:07:15-08:00","id":1475538,"title":"","content":"Also, the Bound. Are the elaborated on in any 1st Ed books? I can't even think where to look, Ruined Temple?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T10:40:04-08:00","id":1475541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1475042-from-the-supernal?p=1475538#post1475538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the Bound. Are the elaborated on in any 1st Ed books? I can't even think where to look, Ruined Temple?</div> </div> </div> </div>Secrets of the Ruined Temple has a short blurb on Bound Horrors that's pretty definitely talking about spirits and the like, and not much else.<br /> <br /> You'll want to check 1e Core p340, as well as Imperial Mysteries's sections on the Alienated entente and Old Gods in general (including speculation that the Rank 7-8 cthonians known as deathlords might be Bound, but the Underworld is slightly different in 2e); Left-Hand Path's discussion on Seer heresies includes mention of them as things the Throne forbids worshipping that aren't the Exarchs (including the example Cult of the Stone Whisper), and its section on the Tremere includes mention in its account of the Suspire that the Seventh Watchtower was one of the Bound until it was freed. That's the bulk of the material from before 1e; 2e's expansion of the Supernal's non-Awakened presence in the setting has generally provided more generally-applicable mechanical systems for the Bound to inhabit and interact with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T11:47:02-08:00","id":1475546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1475042-from-the-supernal?p=1475541#post1475541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e's expansion of the Supernal's non-Awakened presence in the setting has generally provided more generally-applicable mechanical systems for the Bound to inhabit and interact with</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, care to elaborate? I have read 1e and 2e core books, but I'm not sure what you are referring to there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T12:12:49-08:00","id":1475548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1475042-from-the-supernal?p=1475546#post1475546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, care to elaborate? I have read 1e and 2e core books, but I'm not sure what you are referring to there.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, the mechanical backing for the Bound to be typically encountered in was essentially &quot;they lose a point of Mana each day, they can eat Mana from destroyed sources of magic, and reform in their prisons if they run out of Health, Willpower, or Mana,&quot; plus using Emanation Realms' utility as prisons as a reason to leverage their systems and whatever mechanics you could infer from the scattered bits about Atlantean ruins.<br /> <br /> In 2e, especially after Signs of Sorcery built them out further, there are more concrete mechanics for the Bound (who are now explicitly Supernal beings, at least in terms of mechanics), Supernal Verges, Ruins of the Time Before, and Emanation Realms (the last of which hopped to the near side of the Abyss in the edition change).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T17:35:55-08:00","id":1475564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1475042-from-the-supernal?p=1475548#post1475548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Emanation Realms (the last of which hopped to the near side of the Abyss in the edition change).</div> </div> </div> </div>Although Signs does have that reference to the idea that mages speculate Emanations are kind of like halos of the Supernal rippling into the Abyss, and that their Irises are like thin currents that extend to the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> Heck, even Imperial Mysteries has the idea that Emanations contained Irises to places like the Shadow, Astral and inhospitable parts of the material, just didn't quite explore if that made them accessible from the other side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T18:42:18-08:00","id":1475567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1475042-from-the-supernal?p=1475564#post1475564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although Signs does have that reference to the idea that mages speculate Emanations are kind of like halos of the Supernal rippling into the Abyss, and that their Irises are like thin currents that extend to the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> Heck, even Imperial Mysteries has the idea that Emanations contained Irises to places like the Shadow, Astral and inhospitable parts of the material, just didn't quite explore if that made them accessible from the other side.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point being they changed from effectively being the naturally-extant equivalent of Chantries that you could explore as a means of crossing the Abyss without the risk of soul loss to being obscure accessible otherworlds that each had an Iris to the Supernal at their hearts, surrounded by forbidding terrain symbolizing Abyssal corruption, and themselves accessible through the naturally-occurring equivalent of Demesnes.<br /> <br /> The Supernal ecology has changed from 1e, where a credible-enough case could be made by the unaware that it was just the deep-unconscious symbolism that mages used to work magic and little else, and now oddities like the Stygian collectors from Keys to the Supernal Tarot are part of an established class of phenomena and the Awakened create magical places of power in imitation of ones that emerge without their assistance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-28T06:22:49-08:00","id":1475576,"title":"","content":"I need to read up on all of this, but it sounds like <br /> A) summoning supernal beings would be easier in an emanation realm (or at least beings related to the relevant realm) - can they also treat it like an open condition would be for other invisible entities?<br /> B) if you could summon and then break the connection to the supernal (possibly Archmastery) you would go a good deal of the way towards creating a Bound.<br /> <br /> Maybe there are other ways, and easier ways, but turning an emanation realm into a prison for a supernal being sounds within the possibilities of Archmastery.<br /> <br /> EDIT: makes me wonder what is the closest a Master could do. For example, can a Master of Space summon a supernal being to a Pocket Realm and try to turn it into a Pocket Emanation Realm? Can another Master use a Supernal Verge? Is the some specific practice/Arcana which would relate to binding Supernal Beings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-28-2022, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-28T14:53:27-08:00","id":1475596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1475042-from-the-supernal?p=1475576#post1475576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A) summoning supernal beings would be easier in an emanation realm (or at least beings related to the relevant realm)</div> </div> </div> </div>It acts like a Supernal Verge for most purposes and also provides an intrinsic bonus to using Supernal Summoning for those denizens of the Emanation that are modeled as Supernal beings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - can they also treat it like an open condition would be for other invisible entities? </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean by this, since Supernal beings don't use the Manifestation system. Emanations likely qualify as &quot;overlapping regions of reality&quot; in which Supernal beings are fully solid and visible just as they would be in a Supernal Verge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> B) if you could summon and then break the connection to the supernal (possibly Archmastery) you would go a go deal of the way towards creating a Bound. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Breaking the connection to the Supernal&quot; would involve either having it consumed by the Abyss when its time outside of a summoning circle or Verge runs out or replicating the feat of the Celestial Ladder in casting down a Supernal being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe there are other ways, and easier ways, but turning an emanation realm into a prison for a supernal being sounds within the possibilities of Archmastery. </div> </div> </div>This is explicitly the purpose of some Emanation Realms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: makes me wonder what is the closest a Master could do. For example, can a Master of Space summon a supernal being to a Pocket Realm and try to turn it into a Pocket Emanation Realm? Can another Master use a Supernal Verge? Is the some specific practice/Arcana which would relate to binding Supernal Beings? </div> </div> </div>Creating an Emanation Realm is a described Omen (i.e. long-term project prerequisite to Ascension) for the archmaster used as the example of play in Imperial Mysteries' Imperium minigame/chronicle-framing device, and creating a Chantry (i.e. the next-closest thing) requires eight dots in an Arcanum, which is the same threshold you need to pass to be able to create an ochema.<br /> <br /> Commanding Supernal beings is on the list of described capabilities of Sacred Scepters, the sort of Artifact that is personally linked to an Exarch and used to exert authority and dominance over magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-28T15:47:23-08:00","id":1475602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure what you mean by this, since Supernal beings don't use the Manifestation system. Emanations likely qualify as &quot;overlapping regions of reality&quot; in which Supernal beings are fully solid and visible just as they would be in a Supernal Verge </div> </div> </div> That was exactly what i was asking. If ghost/spirits require open conditions to manifest, whereas supernal beings are usually summoned, does an Emanation Realm allow a Supernal Being to exist like it had been summoned, but i didn't think a verge would do the same (only make it easier to summon)... Must re-read the core so. Am i wrong in thinking of verges as iris connecting two things, whereas Realms are things which could be connected to... Or is that right, but i am wrong about which side of a supernal verge the Emanation realm would be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Breaking the connection to the Supernal&quot; </div> </div> </div> To be clear, i mean breaking the Emanation realm's connection. Though obviously if creating an Emanation realm is 8+ dots then presumably making it not an emanation realm would also be...<br /> <br /> So basically aside from using an Artifact of pure Exarch-like control, there is no way to bind a supernal being to the fallen world. (I think replicating the Celestial Ladder is beyond the scope even of an Arch-mage, excepting perhaps if the story happens to be about that...)<br /> <br /> EDIT: so, short of creating an Emanation Realm, the best a double master can do is to Quarentine an already existing Emanation Realm (with Time Mastery to make it like things in Quarentine never existed?) And use it as a private Sanctum - with keyed Irises to wherever you happen to want to connect.<br /> <br /> Or at least that is the closest a Master can get to having a Chantry. Maybe you can summon a supernal being there and then Quarentine it, but it doesn't actually become bound... Although removing a supernal being from the timeline might have some interesting side effects...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-28-2022, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-28T16:18:03-08:00","id":1475603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1475042-from-the-supernal?p=1475602#post1475602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am i wrong in thinking of verges as iris connecting two things, whereas Realms are things which could be connected to... Or is that right, but i am wrong about which side of a supernal verge the Emanation realm would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Verge is a (comparatively small) space in which the power of a Supernal Realm and/or the Abyss is especially strongly manifested and things can get weird, like the Church of the Black Angels where Shades can be called upon to hunt down those who have cheated death by supernatural means; some Verges have a Thura leading to an Emanation Realm at their heart. Insofar as the two are connected, the comparison is a little closer to the pale of a locus and the Shadow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: so, short of creating an Emanation Realm, the best a double master can do is to Quarentine an already existing Emanation Realm (with Time Mastery to make it like things in Quarentine never existed?) And use it as a private Sanctum - with keyed Irises to wherever you happen to want to connect. </div> </div> </div>The trouble here being that Emanation Realms are not subject to the size constraints of a Supernal Verge and Mastery doesn't let you break out of the Advanced Scale chart \u2014 as above, this would be like saying you wanted to make a Spirit Manse the size of the entire Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-01-2022, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-01T01:00:48-08:00","id":1475628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The trouble here being that Emanation Realms are not subject to the size constraints of a Supernal Verge and Mastery doesn't let you break out of the Advanced Scale chart \u2014 as above, this would be like saying you wanted to make a Spirit Manse the size of the entire Shadow. </div> </div> </div>Ah ok, no the trouble is me mistaking what each thing is, and their scale. I think it makes more sense now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}